===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|э́то}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-это.ogg}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-эта.ogg}}
* {{homophones|ru|эта}}

===Determiner===
{{etymid|ru|determiner form}}
{{head|ru|determiner form|head=э́то|g=n-s|demonstrative}}

# {{inflection of|ru|э́тот|id=determiner||n|nom//acc|s}}
#: {{uxi|ru|'''э́то''' [[предложе́ние]]|'''this''' sentence}}

===Pronoun===
{{etymid|ru|pronoun form}}
{{head|ru|pronoun form|head=э́то|g=n-s|demonstrative}}

# {{inflection of|ru|э́тот|id=pronoun||n|nom//acc|s}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[я|Я]] [[хоте́л]] [[отве́тить]] [[на]] [[твоё]] [[сообще́ние]], [[но]] [[не]] [[на]] '''э́то'''.|I meant to reply to your message, but not '''this one'''.}}

===Pronoun===
{{etymid|ru|pronoun}}
{{head|ru|pronoun|head=э́то|g=n-in-s|demonstrative}}

# {{sid|ru|demonstrative}} {{n-g|Generic [[demonstrative pronoun#English|demonstrative pronoun]]. Translated as "[[this]]" or "[[that]]" (or their plural forms, "[[these]]" or "[[those]]"), depending on the context.}}
#: {{ux|ru|'''Э́то''' [[сто́ит]] [[пятьсо́т]] [[рубле́й]], [[а]] [[вот]] '''э́то''' [[сто́ит]] [[семьсо́т]].|'''This''' costs five hundred roubles, and '''this''' costs seven hundred.|footer=(''Translated as "this" when indicating something physically proximal to the speaker.'')}}
#: {{ux|ru|'''Э́то''' [[Вене́ра]], [[а]] [[вот]] '''э́то''' [[самолёт]].|'''That'''<nowiki/>'s Venus, and '''that'''<nowiki/>'s a plane.|footer=(''Translated as "that" when indicating something physically distal to the speaker.'')}}
#: {{ux|ru|'''Э́то''' [[мои́]] [[рису́нки]].|'''These''' are my drawings.|footer=(''Usually translated as "these" or "those" when introducing something as a plural.'')}}
#: {{ux|ru|— [[сегодня|Сего́дня]] [[я]] [[вы́учил]] [[де́сять]] [[но́вых]] [[ру́сских]] [[слов]]. — '''Э́то''' [[отли́чно]]!|— I learnt ten new Russian words today. — '''That'''<nowiki/>'s great!|footer=(''Usually translated as "that" in a response or reaction context, such as to refer to something just mentioned by someone else.'')}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[некоторые|Не́которые]] [[лю́ди]] [[говоря́т]] [[на]] [[несколько|не́скольких]] [[языка́х]]. '''Э́то''' [[позволя́ет]] [[им]] [[ду́мать]] [[и]] [[ви́деть]] [[мир]] [[по-дру́гому]].|Some people can speak several languages. '''This''' allows them to think and see the world differently.|footer=(''Translated as "this" when referring to the content of a phrase just mentioned by the speaker, depicted as having mental proximity to the speaker.'')}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[некоторые|Не́которые]] [[лю́ди]] [[говоря́т]] [[на]] [[несколько|не́скольких]] [[языка́х]], [[но]] '''э́то''' [[не]] [[зна́чит]], [[что]] [[они́]] [[лу́чше]] [[други́х]].|Some people can speak several languages, but '''that''' doesn't mean they're better than anyone else.|footer=(''Translated as "that" when referring to the content of a phrase just mentioned by the speaker while attempting to create mental distance between it and the speaker.'')}}
# {{sid|ru|personal}} {{n-g|Used as a [[personal pronoun#English|personal pronoun]] when not referring to a particular noun. Translated as "[[it]]".}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[некоторые|Не́которые]] [[лю́ди]] [[говоря́т]] [[на]] [[несколько|не́скольких]] [[языка́х]]. Э́то [[позволя́ет]] [[им]] [[ду́мать]] [[и]] [[ви́деть]] [[мир]] [[по-дру́гому]]. '''Э́то''' [[та́кже]] [[мо́жет]] [[расши́рить]] [[возмо́жности]] [[трудоустро́йства]].|Some people can speak several languages. This allows them to think and see the world differently. '''It''' can also expand employment opportunities.}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[не|Не]] [[хо́чется]] [[спать]], [[но]] [[э́то]], [[наве́рное]], [[помо́жет]] [[мне]] [[чу́вствовать]] [[себя́]] [[лу́чше]].|I don't feel like sleeping, but '''it'''<nowiki/>'ll probably help me feel better.}}
# {{lb|ru|{{lg|nominative}} only}} {{n-g|used as a [[personal pronoun#English|personal pronoun]] to indicate that something at the centre of a matter at hand is a certain thing; can be translated as "[[it]]" or "[[he]]", "[[she]]", "[[they]]", as appropriate}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[в смысле|В смы́сле]], '''э́то''' [[мои́]] [[роди́тели]], [[поэ́тому]] [[я]] [[хочу́]] [[им]] [[помо́чь]].|I mean, '''they'''<nowiki/>'re my parents, so I want to help them.}}
# {{n-g|Optionally used after a noun to introduce its definition or explanation. In the most formal texts, separated from the noun by an [[em dash]], or {{m|ru|([[дли́нное]]) [[тире́]]|tr=(dlínnoje) tirɛ́}}. In more informal texts, may be separated by a hyphen ({{m|ru|дефи́с}}), due to typological constraints, or only a space. Often omitted, though usually not when the dash/hyphen is also omitted, to avoid introducing ambiguity.}}
#: {{ux|ru|[[соевый|Со́евое]] [[молоко́]] — ('''э́то''') [[напи́ток]], [[полу́ченный]] [[из]] [[зёрен]] [[со́и]].|Soy milk is a drink derived from soybeans.}}

====Usage notes====
* Regarding {{senseno|ru|demonstrative}}:
** {{anchor|Russian:_overlap}} Although in theory proximal, use of {{m-self|ru|э́то}} overlaps with that of the English distal demonstrative pronoun, ''[[that]]'' (and its plural counterpart, ''[[those]]''). The theoretically distal Russian demonstrative pronoun, {{m|ru|то}}, is restricted to a few mostly grammatically supportive roles.
* Regarding {{senseno|ru|personal}}:
** When a speaker is referring to a particular noun, the gender- or number-appropriate third-person personal pronoun is typically used: {{m|ru|он|pos=masc.}}, {{m|ru|она́|pos=fem.}}, {{m|ru|оно́|pos=neut.}}, {{m|ru|они́|pos=plu.}}, and their case forms. For example, {{m|ru|[[я|Я]] [[попыта́лся]] [[включи́ть]] [[свой]] [[телефо́н]], [[но]] [[он]] [[не]] [[рабо́тает]]|t=I tried to turn on my phone, but it's not working}}.
** {{m-self|ru|это|Э́то}} is generally not used as a {{lg|dummy pronoun}}, unlike English ''[[it]]'', e.g., {{m|ru|[[сложно|Сло́жно]] [[объясни́ть]], [[почему́]] [[она́]] [[мне]] [[нра́вится]]|t=It's hard to explain why I like her}}.

